<Project>

	<!--
		This directory is a dated research snapshot (research/2026-08-roslyn-code-graph), not
		maintained PetBox product code. MSBuild's Directory.Build.props/.Packages.props resolution
		walks UP the directory tree and stops at the first file it finds — the root
		Directory.Build.props (TreatWarningsAsErrors, AnalysisMode=All, EnforceCodeStyleInBuild,
		BannedApiAnalyzers) would otherwise apply to every prototype .csproj under proto/**, even
		though this code was written as throwaway research and never made to satisfy those gates.

		This file's only job is to stop that walk here. It intentionally does NOT
		<Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove(...))" /> the parent (contrast
		tests/Directory.Build.props, which does import it) — no import means the search for
		Directory.Build.props terminates at this file, and the root's rules never reach proto/**.

		Each prototype .csproj under proto/** sets its own TargetFramework/Nullable/ImplicitUsings
		explicitly, so nothing beyond "stop the inheritance" is needed here. Do not add the root's
		analysis/style/banned-API rules back — that would defeat the point of this file. This
		snapshot is not built or gated by CI/pre-push (PetBox.slnx does not reference it — same
		precedent as tools/** in .gitignore); dotnet build on an individual prototype is a manual,
		best-effort exercise, not a maintained build target.
	-->

</Project>
